{"mathdb_id": 356100, "uuid": "b54e74c7-7e4e-4e10-b63f-0ae93fbd59ea", "canonical_url": "https://mathdb.com/p/356100/list-linear-hadwiger-s-conjecture", "title": "List Linear Hadwiger's conjecture", "statement": "Let $K_t$ be the complete graph on $t$ vertices, and call a graph $K_t$-minor-free if it has no $K_t$ minor. A list assignment $L$ assigns a set of permissible colours $L(v)$ to each vertex $v$; a graph is $k$-choosable if it has a proper $L$-colouring for every list assignment with $|L(v)|\geqslant k$. **List Linear Hadwiger's conjecture.** There exists a constant $C>0$ such that for every integer $t\geqslant1$, every $K_t$-minor-free graph is $Ct$-choosable. The ordinary list version of Hadwiger's conjecture is false, but this linear list version remains open.", "statement_completeness": "full", "post_type": "conjecture", "status": "open", "tags": ["graph-minors", "list-colouring"], "importance": "corpus", "source_name": "Yangyan Gu, Yiting Jiang, David R. Wood and Xuding Zhu, “Refined list version of Hadwiger's conjecture”, arXiv:2209.07013 (2022).", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07013", "first_stated_year": 2022, "first_stated_year_source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07013", "documented_by_year": null, "documented_by_source_url": null, "references": "**2 papers in this index state this conjecture** (2022). The statement above is taken from the most recent of them; the others are [arXiv:2203.06718](https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.06718).

